#! 023-warmkeep.patch — the warm resume's full-hit skip, ported from the round-131
#! fork-era patch glm-full-hit-skip (patches/archive/) onto the v1.2.7 ground
#! (round 141 cont. 31-32). The mechanism: the share store's radix keeps a state
#! at the pass's END (at == len, its key the plain prompt's pages — no page
#! follows it, so the lookahead row cannot differ), and an identical re-send
#! installs it and draws without a pass: the warm resume stops re-prefilling
#! the tail chunk (~2,048 rows at d8192, ~1.3 s at the adopted engine's prefill
#! rate — the campaign-20261111-174642 reading 945 ms) and moves toward
#! production's ~212 ms full-hit skip. The four pieces:
#!   1. radix find(): a page-aligned prompt's cap admits its own full length.
#!   2. radix marks(): the full-length tail mark emitted when page-aligned.
#!   3. radix keep(): the end state admitted (at == len; lookahead waived —
#!      the key is the plain prompt; the fork-era token-paste dropped: the end
#!      state has no following page whose KV could differ).
#!   4. engine prefill(): the resume at len installs the state, projects the
#!      held last-row hidden through the head (promptHead — public upstream
#!      now), draws ONE row; the end keep fires after the last chunk's commit
#!      and holdPrompt (the arena final). The follow chunk() routes the same
#!      skip in steps mode (TF_GLM_PROMPT_STEPS unset). The lanes resumeFrom
#!      admits k.at == len. Partial resumes, unaligned lens, the chunked and
#!      pair paths, prompt_logprobs: unchanged.
#! The fork-era receipts stand (campaign-20261101-120948: the gates ALL PASS
#! and the bench held 95 with the mechanism in; the first build's keep never
#! fired — the end-keep hole fixed here the same way: prefill fires it).
#! The warmkeep A/B (the warmkeep phase) re-receipts the mechanism on the
#! v1.2.7 engine: the value gate is the warm-TTFT row moving from ~945 ms
#! toward ~212 ms; the greedy witness 80cc3802… must hold on both arms.



